<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A msg:GetMdibResponse: the first message an SDC SERVICE CONSUMER retrieves, and the one that exercises the
  largest classes in the participant model. Nothing else in tests/data reaches pm:Mdib, pm:MdDescription,
  pm:MdState or pm:MdsDescriptor at all.

  Deliberately included because each is only reachable here:

    * the four-layer CONTAINMENT TREE (Mds / Vmd / Channel / Metric) with descriptors and their matching
      states in pm:MdState, linked by @Handle to @DescriptorHandle.
    * pm:SystemContext with three context descriptors, one of which carries a multi-state: context states use
      @Handle as well as @DescriptorHandle, unlike single states.
    * pm:WorkflowContextState/pm:WorkflowDetail, the whole workflow / order / clinical-info branch, including
      pm:RelevantClinicalInfo and pm:ResultingClinicalInfo (the two element names pm:ClinicalInfo is reached
      under) and both pm:OrderDetail extensions.
    * pm:Sco with a set operation whose ext:Extension carries an mdpws:SafetyReq, which is how glue:R0027 has
      a provider announce the safety information a consumer must transmit. Its mdpws:Selector/@Id values are
      the ones mdpws_safety_info_set_value.xml then references.
    * msg:Retrievability in a descriptor extension, per glue:R0005.
    * the three version counters R0046 ties together: pm:MdDescription/@DescriptionVersion,
      pm:MdState/@StateVersion and pm:Mdib/@MdibVersion.
-->
